00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:30,150
Oh! Emily.

267
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:32,160
Whoo! Emily.

268
00:14:35,330 --> 00:14:38,370
Okay. That's me as a cheerleader. Ta-da!

269
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:44,290
It's no big deal. I have a dentist, you know?

270
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:47,210
I'm gonna go put some ice on it. Excuse me.

271
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:51,840
What do I do now? What do I do now?

272
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:51,840
I think you're done.

273
00:14:53,850 --> 00:14:55,140
Okay, time to take off the bra.

274
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:02,310
Uh, that was really great.

275
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:04,940
But I got to take off, actually.

276
00:15:05,150 --> 00:15:08,070
Take the bra off.

277
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,320
All right, come on, let's go get your coat.

278
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:14,620
Okay.

279
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,370
Rachel's my girlfriend.

280
00:15:21,750 --> 00:15:24,380
So this was really fun.

281
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,250
Oh, yeah, it was real fun.

282
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,300
You know, this bra...

283
00:15:35,930 --> 00:15:38,260
...is really bothering me.

284
00:15:39,890 --> 00:15:41,480
You know, this used to be my bedroom.

285
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:43,140
Yeah.

286
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:47,690
A lot of memories in here. Lot of memories.

287
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:50,230
If these walls could talk, you know what they'd say?

288
00:15:50,610 --> 00:15:52,740
"Want to hear some memories?"

289
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,580
Need a...? Need a little hand there?

290
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:02,790
Oh, no, no, no. No, I got this all under control.

291
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,290
You really don't seem like you do.

292
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:16,720
God. Forget it! Oh, this is...

293
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:22,100
This is not how this was supposed to happen.

294
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:23,690
What was supposed to happen?

295
00:16:25,730 --> 00:16:27,610
Can you not look at me when I say this?

296
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:35,360
I thought that if I could get you here...

297
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:38,740
...I could seduce you.

298
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:48,290
Uh, I don't wear suits to work...

299
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:51,000
...and I bought six of them from you.

300
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:54,920
Well, I'm sorry. I thought you needed them.

301
00:16:56,510 --> 00:17:00,510
My point is, I kept coming back because I wanted to see you.

302
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:03,850
Why?

303
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:03,850
Because I like you.

304
00:17:04,850 --> 00:17:06,560
You like me?

305
00:17:06,810 --> 00:17:08,100
Yeah.

306
00:17:08,270 --> 00:17:13,030
I mean, you're beautiful and smart and sophisticated.

307
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:15,320
A lot of this isn't, you know, based on tonight.

308
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,660
But you like me?

309
00:17:20,030 --> 00:17:24,000
Oh, my God. I can't believe this. All this time, I liked you and you liked me.

310
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,200
Oh!

311
00:17:26,290 --> 00:17:28,040
But...

312
00:17:26,290 --> 00:17:28,040
No don't say "but."

313
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:32,670
"But" is never good. Let's leave it at "I like you and you like me."

314
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,130
Okay, uh...

315
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:38,130
However...

316
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:38,130
No, that's a fancy "but."

317
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:44,470
My marriage, like, just ended.

318
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:48,850
And I'm really not ready to get into anything yet.

319
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,770
But...

320
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,110
I'm sorry. I just need a little time.

321
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,450
Okay.

322
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:09,330
Oh, there you are. I was looking for you before.

323
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:12,540
Joshua's gone, so you and Emily are free to go.

324
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,460
It's okay.

325
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,510
She's still in there enjoying her fake party.

326
00:18:17,670 --> 00:18:21,800
And, uh, it's too late to do any of the stuff I had planned, so...

327
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,180
Ross.

328
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:26,600
I'm sorry. I completely ruined your evening.

329
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:28,640
Ahem. Yeah.

330
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:34,230
Well, if it makes you feel any better, I made a fool of myself.

331
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:37,070
Helps a little.

332
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:42,030
Is there a room on that step for a pathetic loser?

333
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,200
Yeah, have a seat.

334
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:52,710
I'm so sorry.

335
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:53,920
It's okay.

336
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:57,090
I mean, it was just a two-week thing anyway.

337
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,720
I just didn't want it to end this way, you know.

338
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,300
Or maybe you didn't want it to end?

339
00:19:03,470 --> 00:19:05,140
What do you mean?

340
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:07,720
You seem to really like her.

341
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,770
Yeah, I really do.

342
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:15,020
Yeah, but what am I gonna do?

343
00:19:15,190 --> 00:19:17,780
We both agreed it was gonna be a two-week thing.

344
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:19,780
You know? No commitment.

345
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,070
Ross?

346
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:28,910
That girl just spent the entire evening talking to your friends...

347
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:31,660
...asking to hear stories about you...

348
00:19:31,830 --> 00:19:34,420
...looking through Monica's photo albums.

349
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:37,670
I mean, you don't do that if you're just in it for two weeks.

350
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,960
You think?

351
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:45,890
You've got, like, 14 hours until she has to be at the airport.

352
00:19:46,050 --> 00:19:48,510
And you're sitting here in a hallway...

353
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:51,890
...with a 28-year-old cheerleader with a fat lip.

354
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,770
Hey, you're right.

355
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,770
Yeah.

356
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:04,030
Thanks.

357
00:20:08,450 --> 00:20:10,370
What photo album was it?

358
00:20:11,290 --> 00:20:13,920
I don't know. It was you and a bunch of albino kids.

359
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:19,750
Oh, my God. Those weren't albino kids.

360
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:22,010
That was computer camp. Rach.

361
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,760
Hey.

362
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,760
Hey.

363
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:31,430
You're a pathetic loser, right?

364
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:31,430
Oh, yeah.

365
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,190
Hi.

366
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:43,820
Oh, my God. Joshua.

367
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:45,700
Look.

368
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,280
All those things I said about not being ready...

369
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,040
They're not true?

370
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,040
No, they're all true.

371
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:55,870
But...

372
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,750
Oh, I love that "but."

373
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,640
Um, do you want to go inside and get some coffee?

374
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,850
Yeah.

375
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,850
Okay.

376
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:25,030
Every time.

377
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:32,700
Ooh, what do you got there?

378
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:32,700
Pastrami.

379
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:34,660
Yeah.

380
00:21:36,250 --> 00:21:38,830
Hey, you know what goes good with that?

381
00:21:36,250 --> 00:21:38,830
Mm-hm. Corned beef.

382
00:21:40,710 --> 00:21:43,710
Ooh, I was going to say bologna. But that's better.

383
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:47,380
How about a little of that smoked turkey?

384
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:47,380
Okay.

385
00:21:49,550 --> 00:21:51,220
Oh, Mama.

386
00:21:52,470 --> 00:21:55,020
When is the baby due?

387
00:21:52,470 --> 00:21:55,020
Six months.

388
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,770
Hey, now, if a cow should die of natural causes...

389
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:01,020
...I could have one of those, right?

390
00:22:01,190 --> 00:22:03,270
Not if I get there first.

